.Dd @NCOLLECTD_DATE@
.Dt NCOLLECTD-UNBOUND 5
.Os ncollectd @NCOLLECTD_VERSION@
.Sh NAME
.Nm ncollectd-unbound
.Nd Documentation of ncollectd's unbound plugin
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Bd -literal -compact
\fBload-plugin\fP unbound
\fBplugin\fP unbound {
    \fBinstance\fP \fIname\fP {
        \fBhost\fP \fIhost\fP
        \fBport\fP \fIport\fP
        \fBsocket-path\fP \fIpath\fP
        \fBserver-cert\fP \fIfile\fP
        \fBcontrol-key\fP \fIfile\fP
        \fBcontrol-cert\fP \fIfile\fP
        \fBtimeout\fP \fIseconds\fP
        \fBlabel\fP \fIkey\fP \fIvalue\fP
        \fBinterval\fP \fIseconds\fP
        \fBfilter\fP {
            ...
        }
    }
}
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The \fBunbound\fP plugin collect metrics from the Unbound resolver.
.Pp
The configuration consists of one or more \fBinstance\fP blocks:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \fBhost\fP \fIhost\fP
Hostname of the unbound remote control interface to connect.
If the host is not \f(CWlocalhost\fP, \f(CW127.0.0.1\fP or \f(CW::1\fP the
connection uses TLS.
.It \fBport\fP \fIport\fP
Port to connect, the default is \f(CW8953\fP.
.It \fBsocket-path\fP \fIpath\fP
Connect to the unbound remote control unix socket in \fIpath\fP instead of
\fBhost\fP and \fBport\fP.
.It \fBserver-cert\fP \fIfile\fP
File with the server certificate used to verify the server in TLS connections.
For remote hosts the default is \f(CW/etc/unbound/unbound_server.pem\fP.
.It \fBcontrol-key\fP \fIfile\fP
File with the client private key for TLS connections.
If given for a local host the connection uses TLS.
For remote hosts the default is \f(CW/etc/unbound/unbound_control.key\fP.
.It \fBcontrol-cert\fP \fIfile\fP
File with the client certificate for TLS connections.
For remote hosts the default is \f(CW/etc/unbound/unbound_control.pem\fP.
.It \fBtimeout\fP \fIseconds\fP
Timeout for the connection to unbound.
.It \fBlabel\fP \fIkey\fP \fIvalue\fP
Append the label \fIkey\fP=\fIvalue\fP to the submitting metrics.
.It \fBinterval\fP \fIseconds\fP
Sets the interval (in seconds) in which the values will be collected
from this instance.
.It \fBfilter\fP
Configure a filter to modify or drop the metrics.
See \fBFILTER CONFIGURATION\fP in
.Xr ncollectd.conf 5 .
.El
.Sh "SEE ALSO"
.Xr ncollectd 1 ,
.Xr ncollectd.conf 5
